 "blind": true,
 "statement": "Annotated from the Beinecke scan alone (the right-hand wheel of the two-wheel '72v (part)' canvas, with two crops). At the centre stands one clothed figure in a blue cap and a blue-striped garment with wide pleated sleeves, holding a star on a stalk, with a word in a different script beside it. Around it are two rings of nude female figures standing with their feet toward the centre, without tubs, each holding a star on a line and each with a short label; the drawing is faint and uncoloured outside the centre. Two things here are not independent observations. First, which wheel is f72v2: the two wheels on this canvas (this one and the one with a four-legged animal at its centre) have the same label-group sizes, so the line ids cannot tell them apart; I took this one to be f72v2 because the single-wheel canvas matches f72v1 by its ring counts and this wheel is the one next to it in the fold order. If that is wrong, this annotation describes f72v3. Second, the ring counts of eighteen and twelve are taken from the label-group sizes; what I can see is consistent with them but too crowded for a confident count of my own. Labels were paired by ring size and then clockwise from twelve o'clock, an assumption about starting point and direction, so each ring's pairing may be rotated. Per-figure features are generic.",
